-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  intr_exceptions_unhandled.pcpp - Intrinsic compliance: an unguarded raise

  A raise no guard catches ends the program: the runtime prints
  "unhandled exception <code>: <text>" to stderr, after what the program had
  printed, and exits with 1 (research\runtime\api.md "Unhandled"). Nothing
  after the raise runs, so no heap report is printed either.

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    pcpp res\tests\intr_exceptions_unhandled.pcpp -r
    pcpp res\tests\intr_exceptions_unhandled.pcpp -r -t x86_64-linux-gnu   (runs in WSL)
  EXPECT:
    before
    unhandled exception 7: seven
  EXITCODE: 1
  stdout and stderr in the order written; the debug heap report does not run.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe intr_exceptions_unhandled;

begin
  println("before");
  raisecode(7, "seven");
end.
